# Local-only pnpm lockfile. It is never committed, so a git deploy installs with
# npm (package-lock.json) — but `vercel --prod` uploads untracked files too, and
# a stray pnpm-lock.yaml silently switches the build to pnpm. pnpm then needs
# patches/ (excluded above) for `patchedDependencies` and the install dies with
# "ENOENT patches/wouter@3.7.1.patch". Keep CLI deploys on the same package
# manager as the committed tree.
pnpm-lock.yaml
